---
layout: base.njk
title: Notes on job hunting
description: Short, practical posts. New ones added over time.
---
{#- No contactFooter in the front matter: leaving it unset selects the compact dark footer. -#}

<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-head__title">Notes on job hunting</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lead">Short, practical posts. New ones added over time.</p>
</div>

{#- collections.post is every file in src/posts, tagged in src/posts/posts.json:
    Sarah publishes by adding a file, and nothing here changes. reverse because
    Eleventy collects oldest first. A ul so it announces as "list, N items". -#}
<ul class="posts">
  {%- for post in collections.post | reverse %}

  {#- The link is inside the h2, not wrapped around the whole card: wrapping makes
      a screen reader read the date, title and description as one link name. Do not
      "fix" the tap target that way — the card is already tappable edge to edge,
      via the stretched ::after on .post-card__link in pages.css. -#}
  <li class="card post-card">
    <time class="post-card__date" datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | postDate }}</time>
    <h2 class="card__title">
      <a class="post-card__link" href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
    </h2>
    <p class="card__note">{{ post.data.description }}</p>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
